  "motor_policy": "Retain both six-wire pigtails supplied with Arduitronics RU00129. With power disconnected, trace each stock wire to the motor board's M1/M2, GND/VCC and C1/C2 markings. Record cavity numbers, wire gauge and insulation OD, then approve the factory wirelist. Device-end cavity numbering and OEM connector MPN are not established. Quote insulated factory transitions when the stock wire cannot be terminated directly with the specified Core contact. Never force 18 AWG into an unverified stock motor contact.",
  "cytron_policy": "Supply H02 and nine-wire H03 form one sleeved Cytron cable ensemble with TWO Core terminations: J11 for supply and J2 for controls plus four winding outputs. H03 has no supply-positive conductor. J2.5 is signal ground; driver supply current uses J11. Leave J2.10 empty. Neither winding lead is ground.",
  "diy_policy": "A factory-terminated kit avoids maker crimping. For a small DIY quantity, 43030-0007 is Molex's bagged loose-piece alternative to reel 43030-0001 for 20-24 AWG. Use 63828-0200 for the listed 18 AWG / 43030-0038 combination and 63819-0000 for its listed 20-30 AWG contacts. The 18 AWG tool specifies optimal insulation OD 1.60-1.85 mm; the 20-24 AWG tool scope specifies 1.42-1.85 mm. Record the exact wire and measure insulation OD; AWG alone does not establish crimp compatibility. Thick silicone wire may not fit. Pre-crimped leads are another documented option, but verify their exact terminal, gauge, insulation and length; no specific pre-crimp lead MPN is selected here.",
